Track 2: Vanishing-Point Schleife
- Story & Context: Written during a week-long coal strike that plunged the Bremerhaven drydocks into darkness, this track focuses on Greta Vane, a harbor telegraph operator who began transmitting illegal, surrealist love poems over maritime distress frequencies. The song relies on an intricate, fifteen-minute hi-hat solo routed through a capstan-towed tape loop that slowly deteriorates into hiss, echoing Greta's gradual descent into isolation. Between the dry, flickering cymbal taps, a lush symphonic string arrangement blooms like oil spreading over water, anchored by a weeping 12-string guitar line. Over the descending organ chords, Greta’s intercepted voice crackles through the static: "Say again your coordinates, my tongue has turned to salt."
