Track 3: The Unopened Clearance of Captain Voss
- Story & Context: Local legend claims Captain Voss sailed the freighter Hellas into the Weser estuary in late 1975 carrying an undelivered manifest of blank paper, his entire crew silent while the ship's automated horn blasted every forty seconds until it ran aground on a mudflat. This closing epic reconstructs that final voyage using a solemn, funeral-march pulse where every fourth beat is marked by a thunderous tuba blast and a metallic hi-hat splash that echoes for miles. The piece resolves into a trippy, soaring guitar melody that sounds like a siren song echoing off metal cranes, dissolving final tensions into pure atmospheric bliss. The track fades out on a solitary, echoing vocal hook: "We stamped the final letter, but the port had moved away!"
